<title>USA: July Brent crude eases in late U.S. paper dealings.</title>
<headline>July Brent crude eases in late U.S. paper dealings.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Sea Brent crude eased in late U.S. paper trading on Tuesday, traders said.</p>
<p>Nine partial July Brent cargoes changed hands between $19.37 and $19.40 a barrel, down from the IPE settlement of $19.48 a barrel.</p>
<p>June/July traded at plus 13 cents a barrel, down four cents from a deal earlier in the day.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
